policy-capability-sec-channel: TPM2_PolicyCapability supports the SPDM capabilities

Classification: spec-deviation bug fix.

Specification (TPM 2.0 Part 3, version 185, TPM2_PolicyCapability, Table
"Capability Contents"): "TPM_CAP_PUB_KEYS | TPM_PUB_KEY | TPM2B_PUBLIC" and
"TPM_CAP_SPDM_SESSION_INFO | reserved | TPMS_SPDM_SESSION_INFO"; "If the
requested TPM *property* does not exist, the TPM will return `TPM_RC_POLICY`
unless the *operation* is `TPM_EO_NEQ`."

With SEC_CHANNEL_SUPPORT, the reference's TPM2_PolicyCapability has no case for
the two capabilities added in version 184 and returns TPM_RC_VALUE (capability)
for them. The patch adds them: TPM_CAP_PUB_KEYS compares against the
TPM2B_PUBLIC of the TPM SPDM key (the reference has only
TPM_PUB_KEY_TPM_SPDM_00; another key of the TPM_PUB_KEY range does not exist,
a property beyond TPM_PUB_KEY_TPM_SPDM_FF is TPM_RC_VALUE), and
TPM_CAP_SPDM_SESSION_INFO against the TPMS_SPDM_SESSION_INFO of the SPDM
session protecting the command (its reserved property must be 0, as in
TPM2_GetCapability).
diff --git a/TPMCmd/tpm/src/command/EA/PolicyCapability.c b/TPMCmd/tpm/src/command/EA/PolicyCapability.c
--- a/TPMCmd/tpm/src/command/EA/PolicyCapability.c
+++ b/TPMCmd/tpm/src/command/EA/PolicyCapability.c
@@ -46,6 +46,12 @@ TPM2_PolicyCapability(PolicyCapability_In* in  // IN: input parameter list
 #  if ACT_SUPPORT
         TPMS_ACT_DATA act;
 #  endif  // ACT_SUPPORT
+#  if SEC_CHANNEL_SUPPORT
+        // tpm-rs differential testing -- C-ref spec deviation fix (NOT determinism):
+        // the property types of TPM_CAP_PUB_KEYS and TPM_CAP_SPDM_SESSION_INFO.
+        TPM2B_PUBLIC           pubKey;
+        TPMS_SPDM_SESSION_INFO spdmSessionInfo;
+#  endif  // SEC_CHANNEL_SUPPORT
     } propertyUnion;
 
     SESSION*     session;
@@ -185,6 +191,35 @@ TPM2_PolicyCapability(PolicyCapability_In* in  // IN: input parameter list
                 }
                 break;
 #  endif  // ACT_SUPPORT
+#  if SEC_CHANNEL_SUPPORT
+            // tpm-rs differential testing -- C-ref spec deviation fix (NOT
+            // determinism): Part 3, TPM2_PolicyCapability, "Capability Contents"
+            // lists TPM_CAP_PUB_KEYS (TPM_PUB_KEY, TPM2B_PUBLIC) and
+            // TPM_CAP_SPDM_SESSION_INFO (reserved, TPMS_SPDM_SESSION_INFO); the
+            // reference only has the TPM SPDM key TPM_PUB_KEY_TPM_SPDM_00.
+            case TPM_CAP_PUB_KEYS:
+                if(in->property > 0xFF)  // TPM_PUB_KEY_TPM_SPDM_FF
+                    return TPM_RCS_VALUE + RC_PolicyCapability_property;
+                if((TPM_PUB_KEY)in->property == TPM_PUB_KEY_TPM_SPDM_00)
+                {
+                    GetTpmSpdmPubKey(&propertyUnion.pubKey.publicArea);
+                    TPM2B_PUBLIC_Marshal(&propertyUnion.pubKey, &buffer, &bufferSize);
+                    propertySize = (UINT16)(sizeof(propertyData) - bufferSize);
+                }
+                break;
+            case TPM_CAP_SPDM_SESSION_INFO:
+                // The property is reserved, as in TPM2_GetCapability().
+                if(in->property != 0)
+                    return TPM_RCS_VALUE + RC_PolicyCapability_property;
+                if(IsSpdmSessionActive(&propertyUnion.spdmSessionInfo.reqKeyName,
+                                       &propertyUnion.spdmSessionInfo.tpmKeyName))
+                {
+                    TPMS_SPDM_SESSION_INFO_Marshal(
+                        &propertyUnion.spdmSessionInfo, &buffer, &bufferSize);
+                    propertySize = (UINT16)(sizeof(propertyData) - bufferSize);
+                }
+                break;
+#  endif  // SEC_CHANNEL_SUPPORT
             case TPM_CAP_VENDOR_PROPERTY:
                 // vendor property is not implemented
             default:
